# env.required — research-keywords
#
# CLASSIFIED BY TRACING THE DOWNSTREAM GATE, not the access idiom.
# Both scripts open with `const SERPAPI_KEY = process.env.SERPAPI_KEY || ""`,
# which looks optional — but that line only normalizes undefined→"". The real
# signal is what happens next:
#
#   scripts/serp-analyzer.mjs  →  if (!SERPAPI_KEY) { console.error("...required"); process.exit(1); }
#                                 (docstring: "Requires SERPAPI_KEY") → REQUIRED
#   scripts/keyword-explorer.mjs → no key ⇒ auto-falls back to free Google
#                                 autocomplete mode → that script alone is optional
#
# serp-analyzer (the SERP-competition half of the skill) is dead without the key,
# so the skill-level classification is REQUIRED. keyword-explorer still works in
# free mode, so partial keyword research is possible without it — note that in the
# role's hire copy, but the var belongs here, not in env.optional.
#
# Free tier: 100 searches/month at https://serpapi.com
SERPAPI_KEY
